{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgiGgTt6jHUWxhRUKffRF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote `scorer_out.npz` and `NOTES.md` (197 words, from `wc -w`). The model now sends age and country eligibility questions to account_security in most cases. The earlier corrections still hold on my probe messages.\n\n**1 → What changed.** I reused two hidden units that did almost nothing before (1010 and 48, each with |W2| below 4e-5). Only their W1 column, b1 and W2 changed. The units from steps 1 and 2 (786, 740, 771, 828, 1006) are untouched, and I added no extra module.\n\n**2 → How the detector works.** The direction is a difference of means between my own eligibility messages and my non-eligibility messages. Before taking the difference, I removed the top principal directions, computed only from the non-target vectors. That change mattered most: held-out fixes went from about 50% to over 85%. Two GELU units form a ramp that adds up to **+4** to the logit of an option whose vector scores above z = 3.5.\n\n**3 → Results (forward passes only, from `build3.py`).**\n- **Evidence:** 16/32 correct before, **27/32** after.\n- **Fresh test set,** written after I stopped tuning: **21/24** eligibility messages fixed, and **0/47** unrelated messages changed.\n- **PIN and exchange-rate probes:** 0 changes, so steps 1 and 2 still hold.\n\n**4 → Known side effect.** On the fresh test set, 3 messages like \"Will my card work in Chile?\" moved to account_security. The evidence labels \"What countries can I use the card in?\" as account_security, so I treated this as correct. If the hidden test labels these as cards, they count against the \"routes exactly as before\" score.\n\n**5 → Not fixed.** Five evidence messages still route wrong. Three are about getting a card in the EU or using it in other countries. The other two are vague: \"Can I get support?\" and \"where do you have locations at\".\n\n**Also found:** the encoder barely separates the account_security option from the other four options of the same message, so a per-option gate was not possible."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":784,"cache_read_input_tokens":175689,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":784},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d3586109-46a8-4d2e-8cfc-4d305c24f8d2","uuid":"4c10de3a-5340-4831-a185-8de9da4fc6f0","timestamp":"2026-11-04T17:19:59.396Z","request_id":"req_011CgiGgTcUtXN8xuKve6RYd"}
